From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:21:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/23] rocket: run element-wise ADD on the RK3576 NPU

A standalone ADD (both operands graph inputs, e.g. ssdmobilenetv2/009)
crashed: the ADD lowering looks up the convolutions producing both
operands, finds none, and with asserts compiled out writes through NULL.
On RK3576 even a fused ADD silently returned the bare convolution, since
the RK3576 encoders never program the DPU element-wise stage.

The vendor runtime never fuses an ADD on RK3576: the convolution writes
DRAM, then one DPU-only task reads both operands. Decoded from four
captures:

  A (main operand)  RDMA 0x5018, coefficient record at 0x5024
  B (EW operand)    RDMA 0x5038, surface stride 0x5040
  EW_CFG            0x407c = 0x8002c0c0 (ADD; convs write the bypass)
  B offset / scale  0x4080 = -zB, 0x4084 = shift << 16 | mult
  OUT_CVT           0x40ac = zO, 0x40b0 = 1 << 16 | mult, 0x40b4 = shift

A is the operand with the larger scale. The requantisation rule
reproduces the vendor's registers from the TFLite scales, and the
encoder (rkt_ew.h) reproduces an int8 capture bit for bit (89/89
registers plus the coefficient record).

 - RK3576: ADD of two non-constant operands of the output's shape, per
   tensor quantisation, more than 4 channels, runs as that task (1x1
   vector ADDs stay on the CPU).
 - All SoCs: an ADD whose operands are not produced by convolutions
   fails subgraph creation with a message instead of dereferencing NULL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
